To fix the "Minified React error #31" (Objects are not valid as a React child), which typically occurs when an object is rendered where a string is expected, I will implement robust data sanitization in `SmartLessonPlanner.tsx`.

The most likely cause is the AI returning complex objects (e.g., `[{ name: "method" }]`) instead of an array of strings for fields like `methods` or `aids`, or nested objects for `intro` getting passed directly to the state and then rendered. I will ensure all data mapped from the AI response is strictly converted to strings.

